    <summary>Metasequoia IME (水杉输入法): Chinese input method for Windows</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Metasequoia IME (水杉输入法, MSIME) is a Chinese input method for Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS and HarmonyOS. On Windows it is a Text Services Framework input method with its own Server process, a native candidate window and a settings app.

MSIME is short for Metasequoia IME; it has nothing to do with Microsoft IME.

This package runs the released Inno Setup installer silently; the input method is installed machine-wide under Program Files.

## Package parameters

- `/DataDir:` - an empty directory for the input method's data (dictionaries, settings, skins). Without it the installer keeps the directory of an earlier install, or uses `%LOCALAPPDATA%\metasequoiaime-full`.

Example: `choco install msime --params "'/DataDir:D:\msime-data'"`

## Notes

Uninstalling keeps the input method's data directory, including your own dictionary words, settings and skins; upgrading keeps it too. A later install picks it up again by itself only in the default location: the uninstaller forgets a directory given with `/DataDir:`, so pass the same `/DataDir:` again when reinstalling (a directory this input method used before is accepted even though it is not empty). To delete it as well, uninstall from Windows Settings and answer Yes when asked, or run the uninstaller with `/REMOVEDATA`.

Installing as SYSTEM (for example from an RMM tool or a scheduled task) needs `/DataDir:`: without it the installer picks the SYSTEM account's local app data, which lies inside `C:\Windows`, rejects it and the install fails.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>@RELEASE_NOTES_URL@</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="vcredist140" version="14.20" />
      <dependency id="webview2-runtime" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
